record raw-autotune.work.slice-2-synthetic-ramp-suite-and-ablation/1 : work {
    title "Slice 2 — First-principles raw-to-render ground-truth bench"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "src/highlight.rs",
        path "src/oklab.rs",
        path "src/synthetic.rs",
        path "src/tone.rs",
        path "tools/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Replace the reconstruction-only ramp gate with an end-to-end, truth-referenced raw-to-render bench. Generate known scene-linear spectra or RGB fields, map them through an explicit camera matrix and white balance to a Bayer mosaic, apply hard clipping and separately parameterised near-saturation roll-off, then run the same demosaic, reconstruction, colour transform, tone curve, chroma, white-mix, and gamut stages used by production.

        Cover neutral and constant-blue ramps; blue-to-neutral intensity-dependent sky colour; correlated and deliberately non-correlated channel ramps; smooth 0-to-1-to-2-to-3-channel saturation sweeps; foliage/ridge occlusion; a fully clipped core; and sensor-knee cases. Preserve the existing reconstruction-strength ablation and real-frame diagnostics, but make correctness depend on absolute ground truth rather than a vendor JPEG or another raw processor.

        At every production checkpoint measure luminance monotonicity, OKLab error to truth, p90/p99 adjacent a/b steps across clip-state boundaries versus same-state pairs, edge energy, and false-colour area. A test must render through `tone::render` (or the shared renderer-exact stage function): stopping after `highlight::reconstruct` misses the current failure because the real frame's post-reconstruction boundary step passes the old threshold and is then amplified by the tone shoulder. Keep estimator comparisons as ablations, not as truth.
        """
    note """
        The existing synthetic tests exercise `highlight::reconstruct` but stop before the max-channel-weighted tone curve. On `_DSC1289.ARW`, post-reconstruction p90 boundary a/b step was 0.00423, while the immediately post-curve value was 0.01922; this is the test gap the revised bench must close before another reconstruction formula is promoted.
        """
    source {
        kind legacy
        path ".agents/plans/2026-08-07-white-blowout-testing-apparatus.md"
        excerpt """
            - **Owns:** new `src/synthetic.rs` (or `tests/synthetic_ramps.rs`), `src/highlight.rs` tests, `src/oklab.rs` helpers, `tools/ablation.py`.
            - **Does:** fixtures: neutral, constant blue-sky, blue→neutral, sky|foliage, 0→1→2→3 sweep. Each constructs calibrated camera RGB with known chromaticity; runs highlight reconstruction at several strengths; asserts luminance monotonicity, OKLab hue continuity, no discontinuity at clip thresholds, constant-hue preservation until evidence is gone, and fully clipped smoothness.
            - **Depends on:** Slice 1's clip map.
            """
    }
}

